1
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,840
*gripping music*

2
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:21,040
About time.

3
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:23,480
Right, let's get going.

4
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:25,560
No, we go through the back.

5
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:27,680
Come on.

6
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,880
Let's teach 'em a lesson.

7
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,280
Smoke out those red nests.

8
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:37,240
*music turns darker*

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,200
This way.

10
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:50,840
What is it, Strelow?

11
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:04,319
*sounds of fighting*

12
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:06,920
Filthy swine.

13
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,120
Hey!

14
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:17,040
*policeman gasps for breath*

15
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,440
*eerie music*

16
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,520
*rhythmic music*

17
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:35,600
*indistinct whispering*

18
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,400
(Henning) Seen nothing,
heard nothing.

19
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:43,680
*footsteps approaching*

20
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,240
*she whispers indistinctly*

21
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:55,000
That is disconcerting.

22
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,840
Strange.

23
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:04,080
(Gennat) Uncharacteristic.

24
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:08,680
Well, then like it or not,
we must carry on without Inspector Rath.

25
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,280
Would you please summarize the findings

26
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:14,720
in the Dr. Forster case,
Miss Charlotte?

27
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:19,640
Are these the files
seized at his office?

28
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,600
Yes.
(Gennat) Mhm.

29
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,440
Please.

30
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:28,520
Yesterday at 12:15 PM, our colleagues
from Precinct 5 called.

31
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:32,120
Earlier, an anonymous caller claimed
to have seen Dr. Forster

32
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,560
fleeing the crime scene.

33
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:37,520
They followed up on the tip
and subsequently reported to me

34
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:40,880
a fatality at Kurfürstendamm 201.

35
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,400
Dr. Edmund Forster runs

36
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:46,800
a practice for psychiatry
and neurology there.

37
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:50,360
Forster's receptionist,
Miss Sibylle Nachtwey,

38
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:52,400
was found dead in the private quarters
of the clinic.

39
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:56,120
Blunt force trauma resulting in death.

40
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,640
A page is missing here,

41
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,520
January 30th.

42
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:04,920
Strange.

43
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,560
The day of the murder.

44
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,200
Please pass that around.

45
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,440
The matter looks
pretty cut and dried.

46
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:14,720
Young thing,
scantily clad in bed.

47
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:17,680
The doctor loses his head
and flees the scene.

48
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:20,120
We found no evidence

49
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:22,520
placing Dr. Forster
directly at the scene of the crime.

50
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:26,040
Last night, Rath and I
were at the Press Ball.

51
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,280
Why?

52
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:29,920
Off duty.

53
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,880
We were there in a private capacity.

54
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:34,720
And Dr. Forster was present as well?

55
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:35,920
Yes.

56
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:39,400
Gräf and I caught sight of him
for a moment.

57
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:42,160
Matching him to the wanted poster
leaves no doubt.

58
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:44,880
Just a moment later,
he was gone again.

59
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,440
Just like Inspector Rath.

60
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:47,880
Presto chango.

61
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:50,400
We searched everywhere.
(Henning) Again today.

62
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:52,560
Inside and outside.
- Upstairs and down.

63
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:55,040
No sign of Rath.
- Or Forster.

64
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:58,000
He hasn't surfaced all night.

65
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,320
Very well.

66
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,880
As long as we don't hear from Rath,

67
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:05,480
you will continue
to lead the investigation

68
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,480
into Forster and Nachtwey.

69
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:10,040
Forster's residence is under surveillance,

70
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,040
and his wife has been summoned
to the clinic.

71
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,120
(Gennat) Good.

72
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:15,920
You two go through
the calendar thoroughly.

73
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:18,440
Appointments, phone calls, and so forth.

74
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:22,800
Now, this missing page
on the day of the murder

75
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:24,880
seems to be an important clue.

76
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,920
(Henning)
An appointment with the killer

77
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:28,800
seems like the key to me.

78
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:30,440
Yes, it really seems that way.

79
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:32,080
It's the sun that shines and seems.

80
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,760
Dig into it and see if anything
useful turns up.

81
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,840
Of course.
- Thank you.

82
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,120
Is that all?

83
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,560
(Böhm) No.

84
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:43,960
No? Go ahead, then.

85
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:48,840
This morning on Cheruskerstraße,

86
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,200
the bodies of an SA man
and a patrolman were found.

87
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,560
I am aware of that.

88
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:56,440
Cases like that we hand off
to Political.

89
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:00,640
At first glance, it looks
like a political matter.

90
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:03,840
However, we have an initial evaluation
from Identification.

91
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:06,800
According to it, this SA man,
Paul Strelow,

92
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:09,080
was killed with a knife.

93
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:12,640
Our colleague,
Patrolman Hoffmann, on the other hand,

94
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,240
was strangled.

95
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:17,320
One can therefore assume
at least two perpetrators.

96
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:20,960
Given the widespread outrage
over his death here as well,

97
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:25,360
I believe we should
investigate this case ourselves.

98
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,680
(Gennat) There is merit to that.

99
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:29,560
Arrange to take it over
from Political, Herr Böhm.

100
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:31,160
Already done.

101
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,080
Thank you.

102
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,760
Thank you.
(Gennat) Back to work.

103
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:41,760
*somber music*

104
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:43,200
(Böhm) Miss Ritter?

105
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,400
I need to pick something up.

106
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:50,080
(Böhm) After you.
Yes.

107
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,400
Thank you.

108
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:48,320
*music grows more tense*

109
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:17,800
*street sounds*

110
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,520
*she clears her throat*

111
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,480
What do you want?
- I'm supposed to report here.

112
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:45,560
Why?
- I'm starting work here. In the archive.

113
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:48,200
And why didn't you
say so right away?

114
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,320
Name?

115
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:54,120
Doris.
- And?

116
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,880
Przybyszewski.

117
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:58,360
What's your name?

118
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:00,000
Przybyszewski.

119
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,200
I'll spell it.

120
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:04,440
Paula, Richard, Zacharias,
Ypsilon, Bernhard, Ypsilon, Samuel,

121
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:07,200
Zacharias, Emil,
Wilhelm, Samuel, Katharina, Ida?

122
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:08,840
Yes.

123
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:10,560
Wasn't entirely sure.

124
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:13,320
Przybylski.

125
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,680
Przybylski.

126
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:18,520
Paula, Richard,
Zacharias, Ypsilon, Bernhard,

127
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:20,800
Ypsilon, Ludwig,
Samuel, Katharina, Ida?

128
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,040
Just the way it sounds.

129
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:24,720
Come along,
Miss Przybyszewski.

130
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:27,400
(Przybylski)
Here is where we record the speeches.

131
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:30,000
Cut them to disc, as we say.

132
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,520
(Radio) Against the dictatorship.

133
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,600
There is a direct line to the microphones
in the plenary hall,

134
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:37,080
which only we can access.

135
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:41,840
We document and archive
all speeches around the clock.

136
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:45,160
Each disc holds 3 minutes, 30 seconds.

137
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:48,120
At 3 minutes, 25 seconds, right now...

138
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:51,000
the second turntable
must be activated.

139
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,760
*speech on radio continues*

140
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,360
Understood so far?

141
00:09:57,120 --> 00:10:01,080
The first disc is Part 1,
the second Part 2, and so on.

142
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:07,680
This is where you will work,
Miss Przybyszewski.

143
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,720
Doris.

144
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:12,360
And this is how you archive the speeches.

145
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:16,640
Date and time go on the record.

146
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:19,160
And from that,
you get the archive number.

147
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:23,640
Then you slide the disc
into the debate sleeve...

148
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:24,920
*cheerful piano music*

149
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:29,640
and file the sleeve away...
in the proper slot.

150
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:34,480
Here you log the time

151
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:40,040
and place the card in the catalog.

152
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:41,640
Clear.

153
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,320
Well then.

154
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:44,840
Good luck.

155
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,800
Thank you, Herr Przybylski.

156
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,720
Harry.

157
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,520
*music continues*

158
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,640
*music fades out*

159
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:18,280
Why are the Hitlerites
so confident they'll win the election?

160
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,480
They could simply say:

161
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:22,200
'Now that we have power,
we're not giving it back.'

162
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:24,480
Not with the current distribution
of seats in the Reichstag.

163
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:26,800
God knows they don't have a majority.

164
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:30,000
(Litten) Even less among the people.
- From your mouth to God's ear.

165
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:32,360
I think
a grand treat is arriving.

166
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:37,520
With warmest compliments
from Gustl as well, Herr Editor-in-Chief.

167
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,840
Thank you, Franzi.

168
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,280
Oh, Katelbach, please.
What is this about?

169
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,360
I'm not in the mood for celebrating.

170
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:48,880
(Katelbach) Who knows how often
we'll still have the chance

171
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:52,200
to enjoy Austrian Sachertorte
at Gustl's.

172
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:55,000
That's at least
four slices per person.

173
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,440
Not at least.

174
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:58,920
Exactly four slices per person.

175
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,520
Precisely twelve equal slices.

176
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,600
Hold on!

177
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:05,280
What is it?

178
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:09,360
If the leftist parties reach out to each other,

179
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:12,760
as emergency allies, so to speak,

180
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,840
what percentage would they have combined?

181
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:17,480
The Communists
and the Social Democrats?

182
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:19,640
Never gonna happen.
They're sworn enemies.

183
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,560
Yet the parliamentary arithmetic

184
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:24,240
might still make it work.

185
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:26,920
Now then, in the last election in November,

186
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,080
what percentage did the NSDAP get?

187
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,040
33.1 percent.

188
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:35,920
So, a good third of the cake
for the Brownshirts.

189
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:38,000
That's four slices.

190
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,600
And what did the SPD get?

191
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,400
20.4.

192
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:44,600
That's more than two,
let's say three slices.

193
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:50,040
(Heymann) And the KPD,
what did they have?

194
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,200
16.9.

195
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:54,080
(Katelbach) Another two slices.
- (Litten) Two slices.

196
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:56,000
(Katelbach) That makes a total of...

197
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:58,000
37.3.

198
00:12:58,440 --> 00:12:59,960
Or five slices.

199
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:02,400
More than the Nazis.

200
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:05,280
Yes, Katelbach,
but those two parties,

201
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:08,440
or slices of cake,
aren't even on speaking terms.

202
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:10,240
Then we'll just have to change that.

203
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:13,000
Why else did I put the slices together?

204
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:16,520
We must ensure that the SPD and KPD unite.

205
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,800
A united front of the left?

206
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:23,000
If you want to call it that.
- Impossible.

207
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:25,720
Surely it's worth a try.
- (Litten) Yes.

208
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:29,680
You talk to the Communists,

209
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:33,760
and you to the Social Democrats.

210
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:36,600
No, I have a paper to put out,
every single day.

211
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:37,960
No chance.

212
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:41,640
You'll do it, Katelbach.

213
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:44,680
But to build up the necessary pressure, I propose,

214
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:48,960
as I said, a joint appeal

215
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:51,400
from this country's intellectual elite.

216
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,480
Here, please.

217
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:54,920
Don't you want any?

218
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:56,840
Not from the Nazi plate.

219
00:13:58,160 --> 00:14:00,480
(Litten)
Not bad, but...

220
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:01,800
But?

221
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,440
Perhaps some fine-tuning.

222
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:08,000
That's what we're here for.

223
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:15,000
(Ellen) My husband had recurring
long periods of nervousness,

224
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:16,560
of sleeplessness.

225
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:20,160
Yet I had never seen him
like he was recently.

226
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,560
There are private quarters in the back.

227
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:26,040
He spent the night there
whenever work required it.

228
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:29,040
The young woman
we found in bed,

229
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,480
Sibylle Nachtwey...
Yes.

230
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,640
Did you know her?

231
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:35,440
Sibylle was the daughter
of my oldest friend.

232
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:37,800
She was wearing only a nightgown.

233
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:39,960
Why did she spend the night here?

234
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:42,840
She lost her apartment
in early December.

235
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,760
She was supposed to move in February.

236
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:47,840
We found a charming place in Friedenau.

237
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:50,840
You had no reservations about your husband
and Sibylle Nachtwey

238
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:52,600
spending several nights together?

239
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:53,680
Listen to me.

240
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:57,200
This attack was meant for my husband,
not poor Sibylle.

241
00:14:57,920 --> 00:14:59,120
What makes you think that?

242
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:07,920
'We must succeed
in uniting all forces

243
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:11,400
that stand united
in their rejection of fascism.

244
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:14,480
The next opportunity
for this is March 5th.'

245
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:16,480
Final, the final opportunity.

246
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:17,600
(Litten) Very good.

247
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:19,600
And now the addition.

248
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,600
'We issue an appeal to all...'

249
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:24,160
An urgent appeal.

250
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:25,560
An urgent...

251
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:28,120
'An urgent appeal to help ensure

252
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:33,000
that the SPD joins forces with the KPD
in this election campaign.'

253
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:34,400
Period.

254
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,520
No, exclamation point.

255
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:38,720
Strong.
- (Katelbach) Very strong.

256
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:41,920
This belongs on every advertising pillar
in the entire city.

257
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,280
I should say so.

258
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,040
Right then,
who do we want as signatories?

259
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,480
The more prominent, the better.

260
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:54,200
This all has to do
with his time at the military hospital.

261
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:58,480
He was terrified of that time,
afraid of his past.

262
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:03,120
Yet he was forbidden from speaking
about what he experienced.

263
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:06,200
And I am forbidden as well.

264
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:10,720
The hospital where your husband...

265
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:12,600
Pasewalk, west of Stettin.

266
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:16,360
Though you won't find
anything there anymore.

267
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:17,800
Where, then?

268
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:32,440
The lines in question
were underlined by my husband.

269
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:39,080
(Katelbach)
And lastly, Zweig.

270
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:40,680
Stefan or Arnold?

271
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,000
Arnold.
- Stefan.

272
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,840
Arnold. Good.

273
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:49,360
I'll see to getting the gentlemen's consent.

274
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:52,560
Check, please.
- No. Please. No, no.

275
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:55,800
Herr Heymann, you can't pay
for your own birthday cake.

276
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:04,680
Fine, then I'll cover it.

277
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:07,800
Franzi, will you bring
the bill to Herr Litten?

278
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:09,599
With pleasure, Herr Katelbach.

279
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,200
(Litten) Oh!
- (Katelbach) What?

280
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:16,119
(Katelbach) Blimey, bloody hell!

281
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,960
We'd better leave through the back.

282
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:21,119
I'm not going to slink away
like a coward.

283
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:22,480
If you want our appeal
to see the light of day,

284
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:25,240
then follow us.

285
00:17:25,319 --> 00:17:26,480
We'll see each other tomorrow.

286
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,320
You go right, we'll take the left.
- Understood.

287
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:35,280
Until tomorrow.
- Best of luck.

288
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,320
(Hitler)
Proclamation to the German People.

289
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:06,280
Over 14 years have passed
since that ill-fated day

290
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:10,800
when, blinded by domestic
and foreign promises,

291
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:14,520
the German people surrendered the highest goods
of our past, of the Reich,

292
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:20,240
its honor and its freedom,

293
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:24,120
and in doing so lost everything.

294
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,000
Since those days of betrayal,

295
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:29,160
the Almighty has withdrawn
His blessing from our people.

296
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:32,920
In deepest sorrow,

297
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:35,360
millions of Germany's best men
and women

298
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:38,400
from all walks of life watch the nation's unity
sink away

299
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:42,360
and dissolve into a tangle
of partisan political egoism...

300
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:47,360
*mournful string music
drowns out the speech*

301
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:49,640
...of the revolution, a picture
of heartbreaking division.

302
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:12,000
The promised equality and fraternity
were never granted to us,

303
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:17,000
yet our freedom
we have lost.

304
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:18,760
Faithful to the command
of the Field Marshal,

305
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:22,400
we shall begin.

306
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:24,040
May Almighty God take our labor
into His grace,

307
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:28,200
shape our will aright, bless our insight,

308
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:31,800
and bestow upon us the trust of our people.

309
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:35,120
Now, German people,

310
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,800
grant us four years' time,

311
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:42,920
and then judge and sentence us!

312
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:45,440
For we wish to fight
not for ourselves,

313
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:47,200
but for Germany!

314
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:52,280
(Guard) ID, watch,
turn over all jewelry.

315
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:56,120
Empty your pockets.

316
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:59,640
Turn over ID, jewelry, watch.

317
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:01,680
Pockets empty?

318
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:03,920
Whatever you are doing,

319
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,440
it is completely illegal.

320
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:11,040
And you will be held accountable for it.

321
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:13,360
Oh really?
- (Heymann) Yes, indeed.

322
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:14,840
Take a look.

323
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:26,920
*paper rustles*

324
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,320
'Urgent Appeal', is that so.

325
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:35,400
Off to the dark cells.

326
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:39,680
*curious music*

327
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:41,600
(Man) Heymann? Good God!

328
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,560
*shouting and wailing*

329
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:50,200
*door slams shut*

330
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,240
*he sighs*
*music ends*

331
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:18,440
*coughing, wheezing*

332
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:24,080
*snoring*

333
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:33,440
This is outrageous.

334
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:34,600
Hello?

335
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:37,720
(Resident) Quiet. Quiet!
- Where is the night watch?

336
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,680
*agitated murmurs*

337
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:43,640
*resident coughs*

338
00:21:53,120 --> 00:21:55,040
*hurried footsteps*

339
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:57,880
*knocking*

340
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:00,120
Just a moment.

341
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,320
Oh.

342
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:13,120
Chief Inspector, forgive the intrusion.

343
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:15,440
I wanted to speak with you
before the others arrive.

344
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:17,240
Good morning, Miss Charlotte.

345
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:18,400
Good morning.

346
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:20,880
Has Inspector Rath turned up?

347
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:23,600
Not yet.
But this is about something else.

348
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:27,280
I would like to make myself
presentable first.

349
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:29,480
Of course.
And it wouldn't hurt

350
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:31,760
if I could have a bite to eat

351
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:34,640
to get the brain gears turning.

352
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:37,360
Have you had breakfast yet,
Miss Charlotte,

353
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:39,880
or is that no longer done
in your generation?

354
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:41,440
Naturally.
Good.

355
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:44,880
Then please run over to Dobrin's
and get us something.

356
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:46,720
Yes.
They know what I like.

357
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:48,560
Good.
By the time you get back,

358
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:51,520
I might once again have something on my neck

359
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:54,040
that could reasonably be called a face.

360
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:57,720
I'll see to the coffee.
Yes.

361
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:01,840
*he snores*

362
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:09,920
Good morning.

363
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:11,720
So early?

364
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:19,280
And...

365
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:21,840
Your...
No.

366
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:25,240
Inspector Rath
hasn't returned yet.

367
00:23:32,760 --> 00:23:35,200
And you?
At this hour?

368
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:36,360
Pathology.

369
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:39,240
At least you can get an appointment
at this time.

370
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:40,320
Yes.

371
00:23:40,840 --> 00:23:42,720
The new fellow is rather peculiar,
or so I hear.

372
00:23:43,280 --> 00:23:44,280
Mhm.

373
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:50,880
*he clears his throat*

374
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:52,800
*mysterious music*

375
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:55,840
(Potocznik) Have you heard anything
from Herr Heymann?

376
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:58,640
Nothing either?

377
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:02,840
Alright, thank you anyway, yes?
Goodbye.

378
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:04,440
*ominous music*

379
00:24:06,400 --> 00:24:08,680
What, not at home either?
- Apparently not.

380
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:10,560
Not at his mistress's either.

381
00:24:12,360 --> 00:24:14,280
When did you part ways yesterday?

382
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:16,840
Four in the afternoon.
After Mutzbauer's.

383
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:20,320
Heymann turned right, and Litten
and I went the other way.

384
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:23,200
I'll call Dr. Litten.
- That's a good idea.

385
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:26,400
Alright now, out with it.

386
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:28,760
Towards the end of the war,
Dr. Forster had a famous patient.

387
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:32,120
A celebrity, you might say.

388
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:34,440
Well, a very prominent one.

389
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:35,520
Who?

390
00:24:43,640 --> 00:24:44,760
Oh boy.

391
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,200
May I?

392
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:49,920
Go ahead.

393
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:53,760
*lighter clicks*

394
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:56,320
Hitler was admitted
to the Pasewalk hospital in October 1918.

395
00:24:56,480 --> 00:24:58,760
Allegedly blinded in a gas attack.

396
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:01,280
In his book,

397
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:05,840
he calls his time at the hospital
'a dark interlude.'

398
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:10,040
His recovery from blindness

399
00:25:10,120 --> 00:25:11,680
he describes as a 'feat
of his own iron will,

400
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:15,440
so that in this darkest hour
of the German Reich,

401
00:25:15,520 --> 00:25:18,160
he might live for a new purpose.'

402
00:25:18,240 --> 00:25:19,880
The final sentence: 'I, however,
resolved to become a politician.'

403
00:25:19,960 --> 00:25:23,040
Yes, I am familiar with that.

404
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:24,640
You can't open a newspaper anymore
without reading that story.

405
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:27,960
Hitler doesn't mention Dr. Forster
by a single syllable.

406
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:33,560
*he laughs* Does that surprise you?

407
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:35,400
No, because...

408
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:37,440
do you know what Dr. Forster's
specialty was there?

409
00:25:39,560 --> 00:25:43,200
Jog my memory.

410
00:25:43,280 --> 00:25:44,840
In Pasewalk, Dr. Forster ran the ward

411
00:25:45,840 --> 00:25:48,600
for war tremors
and hysterical neurotics.

412
00:25:48,760 --> 00:25:51,440
Are there records of this?

413
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:56,800
All records regarding the military hospitals

414
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:58,440
are kept at the Central Army Archive
in Karlshorst.

415
00:25:58,520 --> 00:26:00,960
Presumably Adolf Hitler's as well.

416
00:26:01,120 --> 00:26:03,520
Yet to examine them,

417
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:05,520
I would need an official letter from you.

418
00:26:05,600 --> 00:26:08,160
The political connection
is blatantly obvious.

419
00:26:11,560 --> 00:26:14,800
It would properly be
a case for Political.

420
00:26:14,960 --> 00:26:17,840
Chief Inspector, Inspector Rath's disappearance

421
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,520
is likely connected
to that of Dr. Forster.

422
00:26:20,600 --> 00:26:23,560
If Councillor Wendt gets his hands
on this case,

423
00:26:23,640 --> 00:26:25,920
I don't expect an impartial outcome.

424
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,320
You don't need to convince me of that.

425
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:30,800
Try your luck.

426
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:37,000
Thank you.

427
00:26:38,760 --> 00:26:39,960
Now let's hear
what the new man has to say.

428
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:43,000
*echoing snapping fingers,
cheering*

429
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,640
*cheers accelerate*

430
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:54,680
(von Levetzow) Very well,

431
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:10,760
let us get straight to the point.

432
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:14,240
The political situation demands
immediate action.

433
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:18,200
In the spirit of our new government,

434
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:21,360
I shall enforce the new political mindset
without hesitation.

435
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:26,840
The system of democratic misguidance
lies behind us.

436
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:32,280
Here as well!

437
00:27:32,880 --> 00:27:33,880
Here as well.

438
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:36,160
I will devote all my energy

439
00:27:37,560 --> 00:27:41,200
to ensuring law and order
prevail in this city.

440
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:46,520
To that end, as of today,

441
00:27:48,520 --> 00:27:51,080
we will enlist
5,000 new national auxiliary forces.

442
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:56,160
And with these men,
we shall be a shining beacon

443
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:59,520
to the people of our Reich capital!

444
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:03,000
Fear no one

445
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:06,680
but God.

446
00:28:08,280 --> 00:28:09,440
Heil Hitler!

447
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:11,560
(scattered) Heil Hitler!

448
00:28:11,920 --> 00:28:13,880
(von Levetzow) Now to the execution.

449
00:28:18,520 --> 00:28:20,200
The personnel will be deployed...
Where on earth is Gräf?

450
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:23,880
No idea.
- ...and equipped.

451
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:26,120
*deliberate music*

452
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:28,560
Herr Gräf.
- Good morning.

453
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:51,080
Do you have an appointment?
- No, but I have a question.

454
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:55,040
Go ahead.

455
00:28:55,120 --> 00:28:56,120
I couldn't obtain
the medical certificate from Dr. Forster.

456
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:05,000
He is currently nowhere to be found.

457
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:07,440
Dr. Forster has disappeared,
yes, we are aware of that.

458
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:10,920
Could you ask Dr. Hirschfeld

459
00:29:11,560 --> 00:29:13,680
whether it might be possible without it...

460
00:29:13,760 --> 00:29:15,520
I mean...

461
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:16,680
if we can manage without the certificate?

462
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:19,640
Unless conditions here
change quickly,

463
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:23,440
Dr. Hirschfeld will not be returning.

464
00:29:23,520 --> 00:29:25,680
And what about all of this?

465
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:29,280
Then we'd all have to join him
in Zurich.

466
00:29:31,160 --> 00:29:33,080
*dramatic music*

467
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:35,040
Excuse me,
the Missing Persons Bureau?

468
00:29:41,520 --> 00:29:43,720
That way.
- Thank you.

469
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:45,080
(Guard)
Keep moving. Let's go!

470
00:29:46,520 --> 00:29:49,320
Next!
Use the other racks as well.

471
00:29:50,480 --> 00:29:53,640
Next!

472
00:29:57,160 --> 00:29:58,360
Grab a rifle and move on!

473
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:02,880
Excuse me, is this where you file
all missing person reports?

474
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:15,800
Yes.

475
00:30:15,960 --> 00:30:17,240
*eerie music*

476
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:20,440
*typewriter clicking*

477
00:30:28,040 --> 00:30:30,240
*phone rings*

478
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:38,800
Karlshorst Archive,
Grundmann speaking.

479
00:30:45,720 --> 00:30:48,240
Detective Inspector Ritter,
Police Headquarters.

480
00:30:48,320 --> 00:30:51,200
You're calling
about a patient file?

481
00:30:51,280 --> 00:30:52,960
Yes, that is correct.
With us, yes?

482
00:30:53,040 --> 00:30:54,720
I just went over all of that.

483
00:30:54,800 --> 00:30:57,040
Just a moment, hold on.
Yes, I'm holding.

484
00:30:57,200 --> 00:30:59,520
Sturmführer Döbrich,

485
00:30:59,600 --> 00:31:00,720
reporting to assist Homicide.

486
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:02,880
Where is the ranking officer?

487
00:31:04,240 --> 00:31:05,960
The Chief Inspector
does not wish to be disturbed.

488
00:31:06,600 --> 00:31:08,960
(Henning) Hey, hold on a minute.

489
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:13,080
*door swings open*

490
00:31:14,360 --> 00:31:16,000
Heil Hitler.

491
00:31:19,560 --> 00:31:20,560
Sturmführer Döbrich,
reporting for duty.

492
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:23,440
Would you like a slice of cake?

493
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:28,880
No, thank you.

494
00:31:30,440 --> 00:31:31,640
Have a seat, Herr Döbrich.

495
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:33,600
I prefer to stand, Inspector.

496
00:31:33,680 --> 00:31:35,640
Chief Inspector.

497
00:31:35,720 --> 00:31:37,000
How can I help you?

498
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:39,520
Aha. That's what I thought.

499
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:45,200
*Grundmann coughs*

500
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:47,440
Miss, are you listening?
Yes.

501
00:31:48,080 --> 00:31:49,600
Inspecting patient records
is no longer permitted here.

502
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:53,480
Goodbye.

503
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:54,640
*oppressive music*

504
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:58,160
*faint car horn*

505
00:32:05,360 --> 00:32:06,960
(Jacoby) It's not so bad.

506
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:12,600
If it doesn't work out now,
it will another time.

507
00:32:12,760 --> 00:32:15,400
Right?
- Fred.

508
00:32:15,480 --> 00:32:17,080
Well, well, quite the sassy couple
coming our way.

509
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:22,240
Nothing can happen to you.

510
00:32:22,320 --> 00:32:23,800
Identification, if you please.

511
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:34,600
The artists, gentlemen.

512
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:37,680
*distant playful trumpet music*

513
00:32:37,760 --> 00:32:39,880
All in order.

514
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:43,040
Well, we're curious to see that, eh?

515
00:32:44,360 --> 00:32:46,200
*patrolmen laugh*

516
00:32:46,280 --> 00:32:47,920
Gräf, Reinhold.

517
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:50,840
Born October 1st, 1899.
- Just a moment, please.

518
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:54,240
(Gräf) Here.

519
00:32:55,320 --> 00:32:56,320
You ought to be familiar with this document?

520
00:32:57,440 --> 00:32:59,440
(affirmative) Mhm. We know it.

521
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:02,040
A transvestite certificate from Hirschfeld.

522
00:33:02,120 --> 00:33:04,520
This certificate permits him
to wear a dress.

523
00:33:04,680 --> 00:33:07,640
(affirmative) Mhm.

524
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:08,800
Born in Dommersleben, Anhalt.

525
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:11,720
(Officer 2) Residence where?
- Torfstraße 9.

526
00:33:12,360 --> 00:33:14,680
Wedding?

527
00:33:14,760 --> 00:33:15,760
He's a Communist on top of it.

528
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:18,360
Being a queen wasn't enough, eh?
*scornful laughter*

529
00:33:18,520 --> 00:33:21,320
By law, you are not permitted
to take action against me.

530
00:33:21,400 --> 00:33:25,200
This does not constitute
causing a public nuisance.

531
00:33:25,280 --> 00:33:27,600
I am licensed to wear a dress.

532
00:33:27,760 --> 00:33:30,280
For now... you are.

533
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,400
For now.

534
00:33:35,160 --> 00:33:36,160
Alright, now off to the other shore
with the two of you,

535
00:33:38,200 --> 00:33:40,640
you pair of poofs.

536
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:42,240
*upbeat music*

537
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:47,240
There you are!

538
00:33:48,320 --> 00:33:50,040
*someone sniffs*

539
00:33:50,120 --> 00:33:51,160
(Jacoby) The police
are standing right outside.

540
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:53,320
(Edwina) Still?
- (Jacoby) Yes, unfortunately.

541
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:55,920
(Edwina) Forgive me,
but we have a bit of a problem.

542
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:59,360
What?
- What?

543
00:33:59,520 --> 00:34:00,960
Mary.

544
00:34:01,120 --> 00:34:02,160
No.
- (Jacoby) Caught a cold?

545
00:34:02,320 --> 00:34:03,680
(Edwina) Worse.
- Dead?

546
00:34:03,760 --> 00:34:05,520
Less terrible.
Ran off to Paris.

547
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:09,239
Just now.

548
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,719
We need a replacement, immediately.

549
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:12,600
Do you know anyone?

550
00:34:13,360 --> 00:34:14,719
(Jacoby) Maybe.

551
00:34:15,360 --> 00:34:16,360
Let me make a call.

552
00:34:17,960 --> 00:34:19,480
*phone rings*

553
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:23,760
Yes, hello?
Fred here.

554
00:34:28,840 --> 00:34:30,280
*boisterous brass band music*

555
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:32,560
When are you going to find
another hangout?

556
00:34:35,520 --> 00:34:37,520
Why?

557
00:34:37,600 --> 00:34:38,679
You and your fops
are ruining everything here.

558
00:34:40,040 --> 00:34:42,560
Calm down, Fred.

559
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:44,760
As you can see,
I like coming here.

560
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:47,000
Do you really think
Hitler will let you get away with this?

561
00:34:47,080 --> 00:34:49,679
He eats out of my hand.

562
00:34:50,239 --> 00:34:52,320
Oh really?
- (Blank) Yes.

563
00:34:52,480 --> 00:34:54,239
Because I do the dirty work for him.

564
00:34:55,679 --> 00:34:57,720
Water under the bridge,
tonight we celebrate!

565
00:34:58,160 --> 00:35:01,040
Miss?
- Ma'am.

566
00:35:04,360 --> 00:35:06,080
Pardon me. My compliments.

567
00:35:07,280 --> 00:35:09,120
You look fantastic.

568
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:13,160
What would you like to drink?

569
00:35:13,240 --> 00:35:14,680
(Gräf) That one there.

570
00:35:16,680 --> 00:35:17,760
I found a replacement for Mary.

571
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:19,960
Reinhold,
let's head to the back.

572
00:35:20,520 --> 00:35:22,280
The air in here is suddenly turning brown.

573
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:23,800
Brown air?
Hold on, what's that supposed to mean?

574
00:35:23,960 --> 00:35:26,400
Always highlighting division
instead of common ground, eh?

575
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:30,280
Where's your sense of humor?
Jacoby!

576
00:35:34,040 --> 00:35:37,200
Your new Chancellor
is spoiling all my fun.

577
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:40,040
Come on, sit down for a moment!

578
00:35:40,120 --> 00:35:42,600
Please.

579
00:35:42,680 --> 00:35:43,680
We're only trying
to pull the wagon out of the mud.

580
00:35:49,240 --> 00:35:52,080
Sure, we make mistakes,
but life goes on, doesn't it?

581
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:56,280
Does it?

582
00:35:56,440 --> 00:35:57,640
Look at it this way,

583
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:01,520
did I let my mood be ruined
over the past 15 years

584
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:04,160
just because you
and your Social Democratic scum

585
00:36:04,240 --> 00:36:06,320
ran your hypocritical politics?

586
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:08,160
You lost the workers
and the destitute long ago.

587
00:36:08,320 --> 00:36:12,160
Did I whine:
'Oh no, those Socialists!

588
00:36:12,320 --> 00:36:14,840
So wicked, them and their yellow press,

589
00:36:14,920 --> 00:36:16,800
the country run by Jews,

590
00:36:16,960 --> 00:36:18,960
parlor communists,
and traitors to the fatherland.'

591
00:36:19,040 --> 00:36:22,080
Did you ever hear me say that? Never!

592
00:36:22,240 --> 00:36:24,280
I came right here
to the Mikado Bar.

593
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:26,520
And I celebrated, with you lot.

594
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:28,640
With all the queer folk of Berlin.

595
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:31,480
*music ends*

596
00:36:31,640 --> 00:36:33,200
*applause*

597
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:38,160
*MC makes an announcement*

598
00:36:39,440 --> 00:36:41,440
Charlotte.
Fred.

599
00:36:41,520 --> 00:36:43,200
What's going on?

600
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:45,040
We had an emergency
and could use your help.

601
00:36:45,920 --> 00:36:48,320
Ah.
Reinhold will explain. Come.

602
00:36:48,400 --> 00:36:51,560
(MC) ...The Lavender Song!
*cheering*

603
00:36:52,200 --> 00:36:54,560
Reinhold. I have no idea
what I'm supposed to do.

604
00:36:54,640 --> 00:36:57,320
Just dance.
You know the song, don't you?

605
00:36:57,400 --> 00:36:59,400
Not my first time here, after all.
- Then let's go.

606
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:01,720
Should I announce you?
Mhm, fine.

607
00:37:01,880 --> 00:37:04,400
*lively music*

608
00:37:04,480 --> 00:37:05,960
*applause*

609
00:37:08,080 --> 00:37:09,600
Ladies and gentlemen,

610
00:37:18,480 --> 00:37:20,240
creatures of the night,

611
00:37:20,960 --> 00:37:22,480
please welcome with me,

612
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:24,720
for the very first time
on a Berlin stage:

613
00:37:24,880 --> 00:37:27,280
Carlo Cavaliere!

614
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:29,640
*applause, cheers*

615
00:37:29,800 --> 00:37:31,440
It's his first time.

616
00:37:37,400 --> 00:37:39,400
So...

617
00:37:39,560 --> 00:37:40,840
be gentle.

618
00:37:41,680 --> 00:37:42,760
*Gräf sings 'Das lila Lied'*

619
00:37:42,840 --> 00:37:44,680
# What do they want? #

620
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:46,480
# Is this culture,
that any soul is shunned? #

621
00:37:47,600 --> 00:37:53,360
# Who's wise and good, yet through whose veins
a different kind of blood runs? #

622
00:37:54,000 --> 00:38:02,200
# That this very class #

623
00:38:03,160 --> 00:38:07,240
# Is outlawed by decree #

624
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:11,760
# Those kindred in emotion, #

625
00:38:11,920 --> 00:38:16,160
# In desire and in glee? #

626
00:38:16,320 --> 00:38:20,080
# And nevertheless #

627
00:38:20,640 --> 00:38:24,760
# Most are proud #

628
00:38:25,400 --> 00:38:29,520
# To be carved from a different wood #

629
00:38:29,680 --> 00:38:31,000
*cheers*

630
00:38:31,160 --> 00:38:39,640
# We are simply different
from the rest #

631
00:38:40,160 --> 00:38:47,960
# Who only love in morals' rigid stride #

632
00:38:48,520 --> 00:38:55,920
# Wandering first through wonders,
curious and wide #

633
00:38:56,080 --> 00:39:01,960
# While all they find
is dull and trite #

634
00:39:02,800 --> 00:39:08,800
# Yet we know not
how their dull world feels #

635
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:14,160
# For we are children
of a different sphere #

636
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:19,120
# We love only the sultry
lavender night #

637
00:39:19,200 --> 00:39:24,040
# Because we are different
from the rest #

638
00:39:24,120 --> 00:39:26,080
*energetic party music*

639
00:39:56,400 --> 00:39:59,040
*music transitions
into cool piano chords*

640
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:27,240
*music turns ominous*

641
00:40:28,120 --> 00:40:29,240
Edgar.

642
00:40:38,600 --> 00:40:39,760
What is it?

643
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:42,000
*

